No need; it's a pretty common occurrence. Monsters can be generated over
the pits just as objects can. You've never seen a food ration or a jackal
or an orc stuck in a hole? A smart mimic, though, might try impersonating
a cream pie or something, encouraging players to try kicking it or falling
through the hole with it. A floating boulder is indeed a bit obvious. :)

Trying to look at it from the bug angle, ordinary holes can often have
objects obscuring them, or be crossed by chaqracters (Dex is the
determinant here, right?). Soko holes operate a litte differently because
of suction, but I guess the downdraft don't affect objects generated in
place.

> Thinking about how to fix this I'm not really sure what should be done.

I take it you're talking about this from a coding standpoint, not
gameplay? For the former, it's doubtful anything needs to be done; in the
latter, daggers, darts, or other missiles; or just fill in the remaining
holes until you can walk right up and smack it.

